  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 228 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nOver the western CONUS, a deep upper-level trough is present and is \nexpected to propagate to the northeast toward the north-central \nCONUS and into the Midwest during the middle of the week. Guidance \nis in good consensus that as the trough tracks northeast it will \nreduce the amplitude of the ridge over the region. The current \nforecasted track of the trough will cause the associated cold front \nto stay well to the north of the region, resulting in dry and \nseasonably warm conditions in the region continuing through the \nentire week. High temperatures will remain in the 70s each day. \n\nEarlier guidance had indicated a potential pattern change at the end \nof the week, but latest model trends indicate stronger confidence \nthat the ridge remains in place through the end of the week. \nYesterday, the NBM and LREF guidances continued to hint at the \npossibility of a cold front coming at the end of the week with IQRs \nof 10-15 degrees for Thursday and Friday, but latest runs have IQRs \nof 5-10 degrees by raising the 25th percentile from being in the 60s \nto being in the low 70s. At the same time, this model trend has also \ndecreased the chance of rain at the end of the week down to 10-30 \npercent on Friday while increasing the chances the following weekend \nahead of the potential cold front.",
